(Step by step) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(1. The employee opens an AI site in the browser.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(2. The PAC file sends that site to the local proxy. Other sites go direct.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(3. The user types a prompt, attaches a file, or sends voice, then presses Send.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(4. The proxy takes the text. A file is read from the recent upload cache.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(   Voice is the transcribed text. Upload alone does not run a decision.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(5. Local regex rules run first. A regex BLOCK stops there. It does not wait) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(   for the Guard Bot.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(6. If regex did not block, the Guard Bot on the Gateway can still decide.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(   The stricter result wins.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
() Tj
0 -16 Td
/F2 12 Tf
(5. The four results) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(Allowed  The prompt goes on to the AI site.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(Warn     The prompt goes on, and the event is marked as a warning.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(Redact   The matched text is replaced with [REDACTED], then sent on.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(Block    The send stops. The chat page shows the block notice.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(         The proxy writes that notice into the site response.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
() Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(Every enforced result is posted to the Gateway and appears in Prompt Logs) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(with the site, the prompt, the action, and the reason.) Tj
