(6. What each proxy part does) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(config_caches_rules   Target sites, guard rules, and the Allow/Warn/Redact/Block decision.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(helpers_prompts       Pulls the prompt text out of each site's request.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(uploads_detect        Remembers a file the user attached, until Send.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(file_policy           Size and type limits for that file.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(extract_office_backend  Reads text from Office and PDF files.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(responses_inject      Writes the block notice into the AI site's reply.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(responses_addon       mitmproxy hook that ties the parts to each request.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
() Tj
0 -16 Td
/F2 12 Tf
(7. Rule example) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(In Create Guard Rule, a short description is turned into one regex.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(The saved rule is that regex, not the description.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(A description of a secret \(pin code, email, phone, card\) must match the) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(secret itself. Pin code is a 4 to 6 digit number, pattern \\b\\d{4,6}\\b.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(It does not match the words pin or code.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(Severity and action \(BLOCK, REDACT, WARN\) are chosen on the same form.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(The test box shows the result before the rule is saved.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
() Tj
0 -16 Td
/F2 12 Tf
(8. What stays on the PC and what stays on the server) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(On the PC: the exe, the local proxy, the PAC file, the certificate,) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(and a cache of the rules so a regex block is immediate.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(On the server: the rule list, the Guard Bot, virtual keys, and Prompt Logs.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(The PC calls the server for rules, for the bot decision, and to store the log.) Tj
